{
  "id": "tarim-77bc",
  "name": "Loulan and the Tarim Basin, 77 BC",
  "description": "Spring of the year a Han envoy is sent west to Loulan, the oasis kingdom of Lop Nur that keeps hostage princes at both the Han and the Xiongnu courts. The Han hold the Hexi Corridor to the Jade Gate; the Xiongnu hold the steppe and the loyalty of Jushi; the Wusun are bound to Han by marriage; the oasis kingdoms of the Silk Road watch both.",
  "provenance": "illustrative: polities, rulers and the political situation follow the standard historical record for 77 BC where it is secure (Emperor Zhao of Han with the regent Huo Guang, Huyandi Chanyu of the Xiongnu, King An'gui of Loulan, the Kunmi Wengguimi of the Wusun); rulers the record does not name are given titles only. Province positions are approximate; populations, development, armies, treasuries, opinions and personalities are game values chosen for play, not historical estimates. Loulan's ruins lie roughly 60 km from the Lop Nur twin's runway (commonly cited position about 40.52 N, 89.91 E).",
  "start_year": -76,
